% This is a placeholder for the 2RC ECM Simulink subsystem.
% In a real MATLAB/Simulink environment, this would be a graphical subsystem
% implementing the 2RC equivalent circuit model using Simulink blocks.

% The subsystem should implement:
% V_ct = OCV(SOC) - I*R0 - V1 - V2
% dV1/dt = -V1/(R1*C1) + I/C1
% dV2/dt = -V2/(R2*C2) + I/C2
%
% Where:
% - OCV(SOC) is the open-circuit voltage as a function of state of charge
% - R0 is the ohmic resistance
% - R1, C1 are the first polarization resistance and capacitance
% - R2, C2 are the second polarization resistance and capacitance (for 2RC model)
% - I is the battery current
% - V1, V2 are the polarization voltages
% - V_ct is the terminal voltage

% For now, we implement a simplified version that can be expanded
% to include degradation mode effects and proper parameterization.

% This file represents the intended structure. Actual implementation requires
% using MATLAB Simulink editor to create the graphical subsystem with:
% - Gain blocks for resistances
% - Integrator or State-Space blocks for RC dynamics
% - Sum blocks for voltage calculations
% - Lookup tables for OCV(SOC)
% - Parameter references to the workspace or data dictionary